  "summary": {
    "derivative_id": "der:rc4:cb_e0f83d5305ed4544a95e72a97c8c424a:summary",
    "text": "Angel Gowns Australia Incorporated is a volunteer-run Australian not-for-profit that handcrafts and distributes garments made from donated wedding dresses. It supplies Angel Gown garments and smaller micro-gowns, tutus made from salvaged tulle, and Early Loss Pouches to hospitals, funeral homes and directly to families. Volunteers act as seamstresses, tutu makers, de\u2011constructors and coordinators; the charity also manages logistics, storage, special garment requests and a database to coordinate supply. Angel Gowns Australia reports nationwide activity and volunteer membership, and its 2020\u201321 annual report states it was servicing 211 hospitals and 102 funeral homes across Australia."
  },
